 ### <kbd>method</kbd> `Topoclass.compute_solar_geometry`
 
 ```python
-compute_solar_geometry()
+compute_solar_geometry(save=None)
 ```
 
+Solar geometry of the points for the project period, saved to outputs/ds_solar.nc (or loaded if the file exists) and kept as self.ds_solar. 
 
+The downscaling does not need it: it computes the solar geometry of each block of points and time steps when it downscales the block. The file is only written when save is True or toposcale.save_solar_geometry is true, for plots and analysis; it holds (points x time steps) values and can be large. 
 
 
 
+**Args:**
+ 
+ - <b>`save`</b> (bool):  write (or load) the file. Default: toposcale.save_solar_geometry (false) 
+
